-- title:
--   Faithfully flat Artin-local lift families over a Noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $n \in \mathbb{N}$, write $P = R[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ for the polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R`, and let $I \le J$ be ideals of $P$ with $J$ maximal. Assume the following lifting hypothesis for $A := P/I$: for every pair of commutative $R$-algebras $T'$, $T$ with $T'$ local Artinian with algebraically closed residue field and $T$ nontrivial, and every surjective $R$-algebra map $p \colon T' \to T$ whose kernel satisfies $\ker p \cdot \mathfrak{m}_{T'} = 0$, every $R$-algebra map $A \to T$ factors through $p$ as $p \circ m'$ for some $R$-algebra map $m' \colon A \to T'$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a family of types $D_N$ ($N \in \mathbb{N}$), each carrying a commutative ring structure, an $R$-algebra structure, and an algebra structure over the truncation $C_N := P/(J^N + JI)$ compatible with the $R$-algebra structures as a scalar tower, such that $D_N$ is faithfully flat as a $C_N$-module, together with $R$-algebra maps $\sigma_N \colon A \to D_N$ satisfying, for all $N$ and all $f \in P$, that $\sigma_N(f \bmod I)$ and the image in $D_N$ of $f \bmod (J^N + JI)$ differ by an element of the ideal of $D_N$ generated by the image of $J^N + I$.
--
--   This is the covering step in an infinitesimal criterion for smoothness over a Noetherian base: the lifting property along small surjections of Artinian local rings with algebraically closed residue field is converted into faithfully flat algebras over the truncations $P/(J^N + JI)$ on which the canonical reductions of $P/I$ are realised modulo $J^N + I$. It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_isNoetherianRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_isNoetherianRing).
